<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-raid Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Cataclysm Classic Phase 3. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c2">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer in Phase 3</span></h2>The philosophy has changed somewhat for selecting gear in Cataclysm Phase 3. While the stat priority remains the same, secondaries are now more of a concern. What this means is that item level, (and therefore intellect), is not always the first and last consideration when selecting gear, and thus some gear choices may not be as obvious at first glance as they were in Phase 1 or Phase 2.<br/>
<br/>Nonetheless, due to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/item-reforging-overview">reforging</a>, many items are still functionally very equivalent to each other and any difference between item rankings amounts to minor optimizations at best. As a general rule of thumb, you should prioritize high ilvl pieces with spirit or haste as secondary stats, (preferably both). As a refresher, the Holy Paladin general stat priority is as follows:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - Intellect directly provides spellpower as well as mana and crit. It is worth up to twice as much as some secondary stats, and should generally be the primary focus when choosing gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit - Due to the prevelance of casting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82327/holy-radiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_divinecircle.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Radiance</span></a> in the raid setting, Holy Paladin is a very mana-hungry spec. When considering Pre-Bis gear, (as opposed to full Raid-BiS), it is generally the correct decision to always go for more spirit over other secondaries, except perhaps haste.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Once mana concerns are addressed, Haste is the main throughput secondary stat. In Pre-Bis gear, this is less of a concern compared to Spirit.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Master works similar to Val'anyr in WotLK, adding a small shield to the recipients of your heals, (though it notably does not apply to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a>, lowering its value significantly). The silver lining is that on the Cataclysm Classic patch, Mastery shields have been able to fully stack and refresh themselves since the expansion's launch.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Mastery and Crit are similarly unattractive for Holy Paladins in Cataclysm, and the choice between them can be rather arbitrary. In general, critical strike is less likely to be valuable then mastery.</div></li></ol>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-pre-raid-bis">Phase 3 Pre-Raid BiS</h4>This is the best possible setup you could have before stepping into a single raid in Phase 3. With the addition of Inferno Protocol dungeons this phase, it is possible to collect raid level gear form the Tier 11 instances without ever stepping foot in them. Some of this available gear is best in slot for Phase 3 even over Heroic Firelands items!<br/>
<br/>The set below should be considered aspirational, as the average player will be able to start collecting Firelands raid gear long before they would have enough <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> to purchase everything included.<br/>
<br/>
